ed by an elision"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element are part of the same syllable, but may have different text formatting. The MusicXML XSD is more strict"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than the DTD in enforcing this by disallowing a second syllabic element unless preceded by an elision element."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The lyric number indicates multiple lines, though a name can be used as well. Common name examples are verse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and chorus."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLyric"}],"title":"MXLLyric"}}}